we've been extremely excited about  apple's upcoming 14 and 16-inch macbook  pros  ever since the m1 max were released back  in november  and have continued to prove that apple  absolutely made the right decision  by switching from intel over to their  very own  apple silicon chips and the craziest  part is that all of that happened  to the three low end max that didn't  receive  any changes other than the actual chip  itself  and the reason we're so excited is  because we're expecting  every single mac with apple silicon  moving forward  to get a complete redesign like the new  imacs  and especially the macbook pros but what  i want to focus on  in this video is the actual performance  of the chip  that's most likely going into the 14 and  16-inch macbook pro  when they get released sometime this  summer and the reason i'm doing this now  is because we finally got some  performance benchmark leaks  that actually seem realistic and match  up to the estimates that i  made based on the performance of the m1  chip  so before we get into those leaks let's  quickly go through the basics of the  m1x chip last year on december 3rd  i released a video discussing my  expectations for the 2021 mac roadmap  including the m1x chip which i said  would be getting a 12 core cpu  and a 16 core integrated gpu my  speculation was based on a very old  report from bloomberg  back in april stating that apple will  use a 12  core 5 nanometer arm chip in a 2021 mac  which is when they thought the very  first apple silicon mac would get  released  well it turned out that the very first  chip was actually the eight  core m1 that came back in november and  because of  that i still believe that the 12 core  version  is coming in the form of the m1x chip  this summer and if you're wondering why  i think it's going to be called the m1x  and not the m2 that's because the m2  name  is almost certainly going to be saved  for the model  with the next generation upgraded cores  built on a three  or four nanometer architecture from tsmc  and i don't think that's happening until  next year so because of that  i believe this new 12 core chip is going  to use the same exact  cores as we currently have in the m1  apple is simply going to add four more  high performance cores  and that's it and because the cores will  be staying the same  the one in the chip title needs to stay  there  so it's gonna be the m one again but  since this is an upgraded version  they're gonna add a letter to the end of  the title  and the one that makes the most sense is  x because apple used x in the past  for their ipad pro chips so i expect  apple to do the same thing  for the m1x since the actual cores  themselves  are identical and i believe that the  graphic scores  will be the same as well but it's going  to have 16 of them  instead of the current 8 and the m1 so  with that out of the way  let me get into how i estimated the  performance of the m1x  and then compare that to the leaked  benchmarks that i'm going to show you in  just a minute  since the m1x will be using the same  exact cores as the m1  i ended up calculating the score per  watt of each of the  individual cores under full sustained  load in cinebench r23  the m1 chip used a total of 14.3 watts  with 13 watts used by the four  performance cores  and just 1.3 watts used by the ford  efficiency course  we ended up getting a total score of  around 7 700  in that cpu benchmark so let's break the  score down  the four efficiency cores used 1.3 watts  which is about 10 of the power of the  four high performance cores so if we  take that 7700 score that we got  and divide it by 10 we end up getting  770 points  from those four efficiency cores and 7  000 points  from the performance course so now let's  take that and apply it to the 12  core m1x chip since that chip is gonna  have double the performance cores  eight instead of four we can take the  seven thousand points from the  performance course  and double it to get fourteen thousand  and then add in  the 770 points from the four efficiency  cores  for a total of fourteen thousand seven  hundred and seventy points  in cinebench r23 that score is  absolutely insane  because it beats out the 12 core desktop  chip  in the 2019 mac pro  and i know you guys are going to say  that you can't just double the score of  the performance cores  because it doesn't scale linearly but  everything is different for apple  silicon  the current m1 chip doesn't even get  close to throttling in the m1 macbook  pro  in fact the fan barely even turns on  after a 10 minute cinebench r23 run and  because of that  i think the 12 core m1x chip is not  gonna throttle either  because the cooling system will be even  better  on the higher end macbook pros so i  think our estimates are totally  realistic  and with that let's take a look at the  benchmark leaks that we recently  received  on the benchmarking website cpu monkey  which showed that the m1x will be  getting a 12 core cpu  and a 16 core gpu layout as we expected  and according to the leaked benchmarks  they're showing the m1x getting 14 450  points  in cinebench r23 which is very close to  our estimate  of 14 770 and surprisingly  that score outperforms the i9  10 900 x desktop chip from intel  which is crazy impressive now some  people have said that that leak was fake  but i actually believe it could be true  because last year a few days before the  apple silicon mac event  cpu monkey actually leaked the  performance of the a14x  chip which is what we thought the m1  would have been named but of course  it ended up being the m1 the leaked  numbers although very optimistic  at the time ended up being really close  to the true performance that we got with  the m1  and then on top of that just the other  day john prosser said that these  m1x leaks from cpu monkey are legit  so because of all of that i think that  we can trust  that 14 450 score for the m1x  and to make this score even crazier it  actually beats out the brand new  ryzen 5900 hx chip from  amd which is said to be the fastest  laptop  chip ever made but it scored about 1350  points  less than this leaked m1x score so with  that out of the way  let's get into the graphics side of the  performance and according to cpu monkey  the m1x's 16 core gpu has around  5.2 teraflops of performance  basically putting it on par with the  very best  radeon pro 5600m graphics option  in the 16-inch macbook pro which by the  way  carries a massive 800 price tag  for that upgrade alone however it seems  like the benchmark leak from cpu monkey  is just an estimate since all they did  was double the performance of the m1  but i actually think that we can  realistically expect  a doubling in performance because of the  efficiency  of the new apple silicon architecture  and if you don't believe me  let me prove it to you the a12 z chip in  the 2020 ipad pro  with an 8 core gpu is able to get  over two times the performance of the  a12 chip  with a 4 core gpu and keep in mind  that they're using the same exact course  the same thing happened with the a10x  chips 12 core gpu  getting over double the graphics  performance of the a10 chip's  six-core gpu once again using the same  exact course  so based on apple's past trends with  graphics performance  i expect the m1x's 16 core gpu  to literally double the performance of  the m1 chip's 8 core gpu  so with that in mind i personally  estimated the m1x  to score around 45 000 points in  geekbench 5's metal test  which basically makes it almost as  powerful as a dedicated  gtx 1080 max q graphics card  built into a modern laptop what i'm  pretty much trying to say is that the  m1x chip  is not only gonna be the fastest laptop  chip ever made but it's actually going  to outperform  a lot of the high-end desktop systems in  terms of processing power  and it's going to have just enough  graphics performance  to play some aaa games without requiring  an egpu which is awesome  so with that said if you've been  thinking about buying a new macbook pro  i would definitely wait for the 14 and  16 inch models coming this summer  because both of them should be able to  get the m1x chip  with its crazy performance hopefully you  enjoyed this video and if you did go  ahead and tap the like button  and if you disagree with my speculations  comment down below  and click the circle above to subscribe  for more videos like this one  definitely check out one of those two  videos right there thanks for watching  and we'll see you in the next video
 

